Title: THE MECHANIC
Author: AI Assistant
Format: Fountain

EXT. SERVICE STATION - DAY

A rusted, forgotten "SERVO" stands in the middle of nowhere. Heat waves shimmer off the asphalt. 

A road stretches through parched desert scrub, cutting a straight line from horizon to horizon. 

An old, battered SEDAN rolls onto the deserted forecourt, its engine sputtering, wheezing, and coughing like a dying beast. 

The car shudders to a violent halt. Smoke wisps from the edges of the bonnet.

BEN (40s), stressed, drenched in sweat, clamber out of the driver's seat. He slams the door in frustration.

From a tin SHED at the rear of the servo, a figure emerges. 

JANIE (12) walks out. She wears grubby denim dungarees over a faded flannel shirt. A socket wrench sticks out of her hip pocket.

JANIE
What's your problem, mate?

BEN
(Surprised, blinking)
I think I might need a mechanic.

JANIE
What's happened?

BEN
I dunno. One minute it was running as smooth as a nut, and then it wasn’t. Is your dad around?

Janie lets out a sharp laugh.

JANIE
I’ll take a squiz.

Ben looks around the desolate area. Stunted weeds grow through deep cracks in the pavement. The afternoon sun beats down brutally.

BEN
Your mum?

Janie shakes her head, smiling. 

As she tilts her head, the harsh sun glints off a tiny, heart-shaped SILVER LOCKET hanging on a thin chain around her neck. 

Engraved on the silver, the name "Janie" shines bright.

BEN (CONT'D)
Are you here on your own, Janie?

Janie shrugs. She avoids the question, steps past him, and reaches through the open driver’s window. 

A loud POP echoes as she pulls the bonnet release.

JANIE
This model has a history.

Janie walks to the front, lifts the heavy bonnet, and stares into the engine compartment. 

Ben steps up next to her, looking at the complex maze of wires and tubes. To him, it looks like a portal to a parallel universe. He sighs.

BEN
Do you know much about cars?

Janie giggles. She reaches back and pulls the heavy socket wrench from her hip pocket with practiced ease.

JANIE
Get in the car and await my signal.

Ben hesitates, looks at the endless, empty desert road, and decides he has nothing left to lose. He gets back into the driver's seat.

Through the windshield, Janie leans deep into the engine bay. She tuts, shaking her head. 

JANIE (CONT'D)
(Calling out)
Right, mate, I suspect it’s a fuel problem, but I’ll need to remove a few bits to get to the cause. Relax, don’t worry. When I’ve finished, I promise it’ll go like a rocket.

Ben sits back, entirely unconvinced, watching her small shoulders work. 

A loud thud echoes as she bangs her fist on the metal fender.

JANIE (CONT'D)
Yup, just as I thought!

She tinkers frantically for a few more seconds, hidden behind the raised bonnet.

JANIE (CONT'D)
Try her now.

Ben turns the key in the ignition. 

The engine instantly ROARS to life, purring perfectly. Ben’s eyes go wide. His heart skips a beat.

Through the gap under the bonnet, Janie makes a swift "cut" sign across her throat with her fingers. 

Ben turns the key off. The engine cuts out smoothly.

Janie dives back under the bonnet, tightening a final few parts, and slams the hood shut with a loud CLANG.

JANIE (CONT'D)
Your all done mate. How far do you have to go?

BEN
About three hundred k. How much do I owe you?

Janie laughs, turns on her heel, and walks back into the dark tin shed. 

CRUNCH of gravel. 

A dusty, branded SERVICE STATION 4WD rolls onto the forecourt, kicking up red dirt. 

A red-faced, heavy-set MAN (50s) climbs out of the truck, wiping sweat from his forehead. He spots Ben.

MAN
Sorry, mate, had to take the wife to town. You look like you might need some help?

BEN
Nah, all good. Janie fixed it for me. She must be worth her weight in gold to you.

The Man freezes. The color instantly drains from his face. His brow furrows deeply.

MAN
Janie?

The Man's eyes fill with sudden, heavy tears. He sags backward, slumping heavily against the side of his 4WD.

Ben stares at him, completely bewildered. 

The Man’s flannel shirt is unbuttoned at the top. 

Ben’s eyes track down to the Man's chest. Caught in the thick curls of his chest hair is a tiny, heart-shaped SILVER LOCKET—identical to the one the girl wore.

A violent wave of goosebumps ripples up Ben's arms. 

He turns his head sharply toward the tin shed. 

The shed door hangs open, swaying gently in the hot desert wind. 

The interior is completely empty, dark, and thick with years of undisturbed dust.

FADE OUT.
